```

- Only **`Student.name`** is updated. The `Student` model has **no duplicate/normalized name field** in `$fillable` (`/home/admin/backend/app/Models/Student.php`).

---

## 4. LINE「綁定」— same issue, stricter campus scope

`LineWebhookController` uses **exact** `where('name', $name)` plus **`CampusID`** for that official account’s campus:

```161:169:backend/app/Http/Controllers/LineWebhookController.php
    private function handleBindingByNameOnly(string $lineUserId, string $name, ?string $replyToken, object $campus): void
    {
        $candidates = Student::where('name', $name)
            ->where('CampusID', $campus->id)
            ->get();

        if ($candidates->isEmpty()) {
            $this->replyMessage($replyToken, "在 {$campus->name} 找不到「{$name}」的學生，請確認姓名是否正確。", $campus);
            return;
        }
```

```228:247:backend/app/Http/Controllers/LineWebhookController.php
    private function handleBindingByName(string $lineUserId, string $name, string $phone, ?string $replyToken, object $campus): void
    {
        $normalized = preg_replace('/[^0-9]/', '', $phone);
        if ($normalized === '') {
            $this->replyMessage($replyToken, "請輸入正確的手機號碼。", $campus);
            return;
        }

        // Scope to this campus
        $candidates = Student::where('name', $name)
            ->where('CampusID', $campus->id)
            ->get();

        $student = null;
        foreach ($candidates as $s) {
            if (!empty($s->Phone) && preg_replace('/[^0-9]/', '', $s->Phone) === $normalized) {
                $student = $s;
                break;
            }
        }
```

- **Name:** regex-captured name is `trim($m[1])` only — still **exact** DB match vs `Student.name`.
- **Phone:** same digit-stripping as parent login.

The UI hint in `ParentPortal.vue` shows the **current** `dashboard.student.name` in the bind instruction:

```382:385:frontend/src/pages/ParentPortal.vue
        <div v-else class="pp-line-unbound">
          <p>尚未綁定 LINE。請加入補習班 LINE 官方帳號，並輸入：</p>
          <code class="pp-bind-code">綁定 {{ dashboard.student?.name || '學生姓名' }} 手機號碼</code>
```

If someone uses an **old** name (screenshot, paper, chat history) after a rename, lookup fails — that is consistent with **exact match**, not with “stale denormalized cache.”

---

## 5. RFID / other flows (not name-based)

`SwipeRfidController` resolves students by **`RFID` + `CampusID` + `enable`**, not by name:

```85:86:backend/app/Http/Controllers/SwipeRfidController.php
            $student = Student::where('RFID', $rfid)->where('CampusID', $campusId)->where('enable', 1)->first();
```

Pending swipe claim uses **`StudentID`**, not name (`PendingSwipeController`).

---

## 6. Caching / denormalized names

- **Student name:** no application-level cache (e.g. `Cache::remember`) found for name lookup on parent/LINE login.
- **`ParentPortalController::resolveSubjectName`** uses a **request-local `static $subjectNameCache`** for **subject** IDs — unrelated to student names.
- **`LearningRecord`:** `student_name` in APIs is attached from **`$record->studentClass->student->name`** (live join), not a separate stored copy in the snippets reviewed.

So “stale data after name change” in this stack is **unlikely** to be a missed cache update; it is **much more consistent with exact-match lookup** on `Student.name` while users still type / paste the **previous** name (or a variant: space, full-width character, homoglyph).

---

## 7. Summary table

| Feature | Fields used | Name normalization | Phone normalization | Campus scope |
|--------|-------------|--------------------|---------------------|--------------|
| Parent portal login (`/parent/login`) | `Student.name`, `Student.Phone` | Input: `trim`; DB: **exact `=`** | Digits only | **None** on name query |
| LINE bind (`LineWebhookController`) | Same + `CampusID` | `trim` on parsed name; **exact `=`** | Digits only | **Yes** (`CampusID`) |
| LINE login (`/parent/login-line`) | `Student.LineID` | N/A | N/A | N/A |
| RFID swipe | `RFID`, `CampusID`, `enable` | N/A | N/A | Yes |
| `StudentController::update` | Updates `Student.name` only | As sent by client | Stored as provided | N/A |

**Practical implication for the reported bug (e.g. card showing「林澤清 國中一年級(J1) 延平」):** any flow that matches **literal `Student.name`** will break if the row was renamed but the user still binds with the **old** string. There is **no** second “binding name” column to refresh; fixing behavior would be a **product/code change** (fuzzy match, alternate names, or bind-by-id/phone-only), not something this investigation found as an existing denormalized cache layer.

